If an item in the 'probes' list is not a dictionary (e.g., due to malformed JSON input), calling item.get() will raise an AttributeError. We should check that each item is a dictionary before calling .get() to prevent unhandled exceptions and fail closed gracefully.

```suggestion
    for item in probes:
        if not isinstance(item, dict):
            errors.append("invalid_probe_type")
            continue
        if item.get("expected") != item.get("observed"):
```
